02,"_39":103,"_41":42,"_43":42,"_44":42,"_45":104,"_47":42,"_48":105,"_50":106,"_52":107,"_54":108,"_55":109,"_57":110,"_59":111,"_61":112,"_63":42,"_64":65},{"_25":81,"_27":82,"_29":30,"_31":83,"_33":84,"_35":85,"_37":86,"_39":87,"_41":42,"_43":42,"_44":42,"_45":88,"_47":42,"_48":89,"_50":90,"_52":91,"_54":-5,"_55":92,"_57":93,"_59":94,"_61":95,"_63":42,"_64":65},{"_25":26,"_27":28,"_29":30,"_31":32,"_33":34,"_35":36,"_37":38,"_39":40,"_41":42,"_43":42,"_44":42,"_45":46,"_47":42,"_48":49,"_50":51,"_52":53,"_54":-5,"_55":56,"_57":58,"_59":60,"_61":62,"_63":42,"_64":65},"id","1175","name","The Treaty of Paris","type","event","startDescription","This agreement marked the end of the American Revolutionary War, establishing peace between Great Britain and the United States.","endDescription","The treaty was significant in recognizing American independence and establishing borders.","startYear",1783,"startMonth",9,"startDay",3,"endYear",0,"endMonth","endDay","startSignificance",0.9,"endSignificance","imageUrl","https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/25/Treaty_of_Paris_%281783%29.jpg/330px-Treaty_of_Paris_%281783%29.jpg","imageCredit","Image: Treaty of Paris (1783) / Wikimedia Commons","sourceUrl","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Treaty_of_Paris_(1783)","cdnId","country",{"_27":78,"_79":80},"subjects",[72,73],"group",{"_27":69,"_70":71},"user",{"_25":66,"_67":68},"likes","liked",false,"6","username","HistOracle","Colonial North America","icon","GiTreasureMap",{"_25":76,"_27":77},{"_25":74,"_27":75},"2","politics","1","military","United States of America","continent","NorthAmerica","1482","Declaration of Independence","A pivotal document asserting the colonies' intent to separate from British rule, outlining grievances and the philosophy of governance.","The declaration marked the official beginning of the United States as a sovereign nation, influencing future democratic movements.",1776,7,4,1,"","Image: Declaration of independence / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Declaration_of_Independence",{"_27":78,"_79":80},[96],{"_27":69,"_70":71},{"_25":66,"_67":68},{"_25":74,"_27":75},"544","The Boston Tea Party","A political protest by the American colonists against British taxation, where tea was dumped into Boston Harbor.","This act of defiance became a pivotal moment in the lead-up to the American Revolution.",1773,12,16,0.8,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Boston_Tea_Party_w.jpg/330px-Boston_Tea_Party_w.jpg","W.D. Cooper. \"Boston Tea Party.\" / E. Newberry / Library of Congress / Wikimedia Commons / Public domain","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boston_Tea_Party","images/67df9c878c1d31971a1800b961f99678a88cdf62.webp",{"_27":78,"_79":80},[113,114],{"_27":69,"_70":71},{"_25":66,"_67":68},{"_25":74,"_27":75},{"_25":115,"_27":116},"3","culture","566","The Boston Massacre","This confrontation between British soldiers and American colonists resulted in the deaths of five colonists, escalating tensions leading to the American Revolution.","The event became a rallying point for colonial resistance against British rule, symbolizing the struggle for independence.",1770,5,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6d/The_Boston_Massacre_MET_DT2086.jpg/330px-The_Boston_Massacre_MET_DT2086.jpg","Paul Revere / Wikimedia Commons / Public domain","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boston_Massacre","images/92d04c0f26abdc730e0da70dcfdf6b885790958c.webp",{"_27":78,"_79":80},[131,132],{"_27":69,"_70":71},{"_25":66,"_67":68},{"_25":74,"_27":75},{"_25":115,"_27":116},"1686","The French and Indian War","A conflict between Britain and France in North America, part of the larger Seven Years' War, marked by battles over territory and resources.","The war concluded with the signing of the Treaty of Paris, significantly altering the territorial claims in North America.",1754,28,1763,2,10,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/French_and_indian_war_map.svg/330px-French_and_indian_war_map.svg.png","Image: French and Indian War / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/French_and_Indian_War",{"_27":78,"_79":80},[149,150],{"_27":69,"_70":71},{"_25":66,"_67":68},{"_25":76,"_27":77},{"_25":74,"_27":75},"875","Thomas Jefferson","person","A founding father and the principal author of the Declaration of Independence, he played a crucial role in the early development of the United States.","His legacy includes the promotion of individual liberty and the separation of church and state, influencing future generations.",1743,13,1826,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Official_Presidential_portrait_of_Thomas_Jefferson_%28by_Rembrandt_Peale%2C_1800%29.jpg/330px-Official_Presidential_portrait_of_Thomas_Jefferson_%28by_Rembrandt_Peale%2C_1800%29.jpg","Image: Thomas Jefferson / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Jefferson",{"_27":78,"_79":80},[166,167],{"_27":69,"_70":71},{"_25":66,"_67":68},{"_25":74,"_27":75},{"_25":168,"_27":169},"4","intellectual","1685","The Great Awakening","period","A series of religious revivals that swept through the American colonies, emphasizing personal faith and emotional connection to religion.","The movement waned, but it left a lasting impact on American religion and society, fostering a spirit of independence.",1730,1755,0.7,0.6,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/92/Sinners_in_the_Hands_of_an_Angry_God_by_Jonathan_Edwards_1741.jpg/330px-Sinners_in_the_Hands_of_an_Angry_God_by_Jonathan_Edwards_1741.jpg","Image: First Great Awakening / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First_Great_Awakening",{"_27":78,"_79":80},[186,187],{"_27":69,"_70":71},{"_25":66,"_67":68},{"_25":115,"_27":116},{"_25":188,"_27":189},"7","religion","882","Benjamin Franklin","A polymath who made significant contributions to various fields including science, politics, and philosophy. He was instrumental in the American Enlightenment and the founding of the United States.","His legacy continues to influence American culture and politics, with his ideas on democracy, civic responsibility, and scientific inquiry remaining relevant.",1706,17,1790,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Joseph_Siffrein_Duplessis_-_Benjamin_Franklin_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg/330px-Joseph_Siffrein_Duplessis_-_Benjamin_Franklin_-_Google_Art_Project.jpg","Image: Benjamin Franklin / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Benjamin_Franklin",{"_27":78,"_79":80},[204,205],{"_27":69,"_70":71},{"_25":66,"_67":68},{"_25":74,"_27":75},{"_25":168,"_27":169},"1684","The Navigation Acts","A series of laws that restricted colonial trade to England and its colonies, aiming to bolster the British economy.","The acts were increasingly resisted by colonists, contributing to growing tensions that eventually led to revolution.",1651,1733,"Image: Navigation Acts / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Navigation_Acts",{"_27":78,"_79":80},[218,219],{"_27":69,"_70":71},{"_25":66,"_67":68},{"_25":74,"_27":75},{"_25":220,"_27":221},"8","economic","1151","American Frontier","The American Frontier represents the westward expansion of settlers and the development of new territories in the United States.","The era concluded as the frontier was declared closed, marking a significant shift in American society and policy.",1607,1912,"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/The_Cow_Boy_1888.jpg/330px-The_Cow_Boy_1888.jpg","Image: American frontier / Wikimedia Commons","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Frontier",{"_27":78,"_79":80},[235],{"_27":69,"_70":71},{"_25":66,"_67":68},{"_25":115,"_27":116},[],"subject",[],[],"yearStart",-300000,"yearEnd",2025,"search","sortBy",true,45]
